      "created": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
      "modified": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
      "name": "Cloud data exfiltration: leaked SSH key to S3 training-data theft",
      "description": "A private key pushed to GitHub is used to log into an EC2 dev host. The intruder steals the instance role credentials from IMDSv2, enumerates IAM and S3, syncs a training-data bucket to the host and exfiltrates it over SFTP. All times are original capture times on 2026-10-13 UTC and are shifted on replay. Correlates github_audit, linux_auth, crowdstrike_fdr, aws_cloudtrail and aws_vpc_flow.",
      "scope": "incident",
      "start_refs": [
        "attack-action--e86d395e-f60a-5594-93c3-a66eb1353995"
      ],
      "extensions": {
        "extension-definition--fb9c968a-745b-4ade-9b25-c324172197f4": {
